instruction:
The shop's SQLite database /app/shopdb/shop.db is at schema version 2 (migrations 001 and 002 are applied). Bring it up to date: apply the pending migrations in /app/shopdb/migrations with /app/shopdb/migrate.py, fixing the migration runner and the migrations where they are wrong. When you are done:
- every migration file in migrations/ is applied exactly once and recorded in schema_migrations;
- orders.total_cents holds each order's total in whole cents as an INTEGER (19.99 -> 1999);
- no customer or order is lost, duplicated or changed;
- running migrate.py on an empty database (SHOPDB=/path/to/new.db) builds the same schema and data from scratch, and running it on an up-to-date database changes nothing;
- a migration that has been applied to shop.db is never edited afterwards (001 and 002 already are).

Then write /app/shopdb/out/top_customers.csv with `python3 /app/shopdb/report.py`.
